                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[i]Age of Enigma[/i] is a decent casual collection of diverse minigames/puzzles connected by a linear ghost story. It took me ~3 hours. The game resolution is fixed at 1024x768 (fullscreen or windowed).\n\nThere are \"casual\" and \"adventure\" modes, I played the latter and still found it fairly casual. The game's decent, the art is decent, the sounds are decent, the voiceovers, hmm, the shadow guy may be a little below par. I couldn't find anything outstanding about this game, either positively or negatively. It is no hidden object game, but in many respects similar to one.\n\nIt's ok if you like that sort of thing and can pick it up cheaply (I got it in a bundle), but otherwise, I wouldn't recommend it. If you're looking for a casual puzzle game with excellent art and writing, check out [url=http://store.steampowered.com/app/31270/]Puzzle Agent[/url] instead - it's better, cheaper, and funnier (and also a little mysterious and scary). If you want to be truly amazed by a casual puzzle game, get [url=http://store.steampowered.com/app/288160/]The Room[/url].",
